Changelog: 22-11-2026 23:04:34

Fixed. The text of the README, install.sh, run.sh and the window is rewritten to the writing standard: short sentences,
one fact each, and a list where the README's introduction and the info text name three or more things. The info text
names the sliders by their labels. install.sh says the app is removed, not uninstalled, and writes anymore. No labels
were renamed and no facts were corrected. Nothing the app does has changed. No tests changed.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 16:58:55

Fixed. The checkbox reads Keep the audio link awake, and its tooltip says that it plays a silent loop while the window
is open, as CLAUDE.md asks. The label held that text before.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 10:09:36

Breaking. Windows support is removed (owner, 15-11-2026): no run.ps1, and run.sh uses .venv-linux.

Breaking. No VERSION (owner, 15-11-2026): a development app is never released, so its header names the checkout's
last commit and its time ("5fb1aa8 · 15-11-2026 07:20", core's nexus.header()) where it showed a version, and
--version prints the same.

